Follow buttons across the app had no working handlers, and the Edit Profile button had no `onClick`. This adds end-to-end follow/unfollow support and a functional edit profile modal.

## Backend

- **`follow.controller.js`**: Fixed missing `createNotification` import (was called but never imported — runtime error on every follow). Added `checkIfFollowing` controller.
- **`follow.routes.js`**: Added `GET /:userId/check` with `apiLimiter` + auth, placed before parameterized routes to avoid shadowing.

## Client — Services & Hooks

- **`services/index.js`**: Added `followService.checkIfFollowing(userId)` → `GET /follow/:userId/check`.
- **`hooks/useFollow.js`** *(new)*: `toggleFollow(userId, isCurrentlyFollowing)` — calls backend toggle, dispatches `updateFollowStatus` to Redux, shows success/error toast.
- **`hooks/index.js`**: Exports `useFollow`.

## Client — Components & Pages

- **`EditProfileModal.jsx`** *(new)*: Modal for updating bio (200-char limit) and profile image URL with live preview. Submits via `userService.updateProfile`, dispatches `fetchUserSuccess` to Redux.
- **`Profile.jsx`**: Own profile → Edit Profile button opens modal. Other users → Follow/Unfollow button with state seeded from `checkIfFollowing` on mount.
- **`Search.jsx`**: Replaces static "View Profile" button with Follow/Unfollow. Avatar/username are `Link`s to profile. Follow statuses fetched concurrently via `Promise.all`.

```js
// Before: button with no handler
<button className="...">View Profile</button>

// After: stateful follow toggle per result
<button onClick={() => handleFollowClick(user._id)} className={isFollowing ? '...' : '...'}>
  {isFollowing ? 'Unfollow' : 'Follow'}
</button>
```

